## 6. Timeouts

| Wait | Value | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Conversion, first launch | 30 s | The real answer lands in 4–6 s when the flow is right. |
| Conversion, returning launch | 10 s | |
| Conversion, re-ask after an empty answer | 8 s | Then GCD. |
| Deferred deep link | 5 s | In parallel with the conversion, never after it. |
| Organic re-check delay before GCD | 5 s | `af_status=Organic` on a first run is often a false positive. |
| GCD HTTP | 10 s | |
| Config endpoint | 15 s | |
| Instant connectivity check | 0 | `activeNetwork` only. Used for the first frame. |
| Connectivity grace inside a decision | ~3 s | For a link that is still coming up. |

---

## 7. Proving it works

Watch the right tags. A filter that omits the attribution and config classes
hides exactly the lines that matter:

```powershell
adb logcat -c; adb logcat -s <Router>:V <Tracker>:V <ConfigClient>:V <Offline>:V
```

Do this on a **debug** build, or temporarily drop `public static *** i(...)` from
the `-assumenosideeffects android.util.Log` block — release strips exactly the
lines this section asks you to read.

A healthy OneLink first launch reads like this, end to end in under ten
seconds:

```
mode=unset -> first decision
AppsFlyer started from <Router>, uid=1785315478281-...
deep link params: {deep_link_value=..., is_deferred=true}
onConversionDataSuccess: {af_status=Non-organic, campaign=..., media_source=...}
conversion={af_status=Non-organic, ...}
POST https://<endpoint>  body {"af_status":"Non-organic", ... "af_id":"...", "push_token":"..."}
HTTP 200 body={"ok":true,"url":"https://..."}
```

Red flags, each mapping to a section above:

| In the log | Means |
|---|---|
| `conversion={}` returned in a few ms | A cached failure from an offline start. §2 |
| 30 s gap, then `onBecameForeground` | `init` ran too late or `start` got the app context. §1 |
| `GCD HTTP 400 {"error_reason":"The 'devkey' query parameter is not found"}` | The dev key went into a header instead of the query string. Pitfalls #37 |
| `GCD HTTP 400` with any other reason | AppsFlyer has no such install yet — the launch never went out. §1, §2 |
| `af_status=Organic` on a OneLink install | The GCD re-check should overrule it; if it doesn't, check the key and bundle. |
| `HTTP 404 {"ok":false}` with an empty body of attribution fields | Not a backend bug. Fix the attribution, not the endpoint. |

Test matrix for the launch, all on a real device with `adb shell pm clear`
between runs: OneLink install online; OneLink install with the radio off, then
on; organic install; returning gray user; returning native user; cold push;
warm push; airplane mode mid-session.
